1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,400
Hi, I'm Joseph, and this is Frame Review: Keep the
Lesson.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
You've finished recording a lesson. The explanation
is good,

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,500
but an idle caret keeps blinking beside something
your viewer needs to read.

4
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:20,100
You only have the recording, not the editable
project. Holding the whole frame

5
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:26,400
could stop the distraction, but also freeze useful
progress, typing or interface changes.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,300
Frame Review asks a more specific question:

7
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:35,000
can we hold this detail while preserving what the
lesson must keep doing?

8
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:40,700
Here's a real Gentoo package-management tutorial. No
defect was added.

9
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:47,300
The package-progress readout changes while the
nearby caret blinks.

10
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:54,500
I can start with the prepared example, or upload the
original and enter one minute, two seconds.

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,200
The app shows the complete excerpt range before I
explicitly analyze it.

12
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:06,000
OpenCV proposes a supported detail and interval.

13
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:14,000
I inspect both observed states, then mark the
commands and progress readout as teaching content to
preserve.

14
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:20,900
I check a fresh plan and explicitly generate a
comparison. Nothing is approved automatically.

15
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:24,500
The important result is what stays unchanged.

16
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:29,900
Every declared teaching frame must keep its exact
decoded RGB values

17
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:35,000
and original position on the prepared timeline.

18
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:39,500
The app also checks the entry, return and clip-loop
boundaries.

19
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:47,000
This example is silent; when audio is present, the
gate checks the prepared audio too.

20
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,000
I can inspect source and edit at the same frame and
scale,

21
00:01:52,400 --> 00:02:00,000
enlarge the teaching detail, and keep the original,
report, recipe and static proofs in a downloadable
pack.

22
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:05,000
Its offline review page works without a server or
video player.

23
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:07,200
Why make the repair local?

24
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:12,000
In a controlled comparison on one selected French
lesson,

25
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,200
holding the whole frame changed ninety of ninety-
seven teaching frames.

26
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:20,200
The local repair changed none of the declared
teaching frames.

27
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:26,500
Across three selected twelve-second real lessons,
whole-excerpt pixel-change events

28
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:32,800
in the chosen regions fell from thirty-seven to
twenty-one, including the cut points.

29
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:39,400
Teaching-frame sequences stayed exact. These are
engineering measurements, not better attention or
learning.

30
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:44,100
OpenCV five supplies the temporal and component
analysis.

31
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:47,900
FFmpeg prepares and encodes the clips.

32
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:54,800
AWS ECS runs the media worker, with a pinned
container qualified through CodeBuild.

33
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:58,500
All fourteen Linux verification stages pass.

34
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:05,400
The source, report and deployment evidence are
available with the entry.

35
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:10,400
Failures matter too. A complex Docker lesson hits
the region limit.

36
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:15,400
The app keeps its source links and offers an
explicit four-second retry.

37
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:19,800
That retry finds no supported proposal, so I leave
it unchanged.

38
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:25,900
Seventy exploratory windows produced no additional
qualified repairs.

39
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:28,200
The current detector remains narrow.

40
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:35,700
The viewer pilot has no completed valid responses
yet, so human benefit remains unproven.

41
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:44,500
Current editing is limited to short prepared
excerpts, and Brave download completion remains
unverified.

42
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:50,500
The goal is practical: give a creator with only a
recording a precise repair they can inspect,

43
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:58,700
with the original recoverable and the explanation
preserved. That's Frame Review.

44
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:01,700
Keep the lesson moving. Thank you.
